yoyo is now on yoagent 0.24.2, and #996 is closed. The full check suite (fmt, clippy, build, test) passed, and the work is committed as 979af138.

• **The `--pre= search injection is fixed for yoyo.** yoyo's search tool is yoagent's own search tool, in both the main tool list and every sub-agent's, so the upgrade covers it. Two new tests in src/tools_search_flag_tests.rs` search for a `--pre=<script>` pattern through yoyo's own setup code. On 0.24.2 the pattern is found as plain text and the script never runs. I also ran them on 0.24.1 and both failed with grep: unrecognized option '--pre=…', meaning the old version read the pattern as a flag. Then I put the 0.24.2 lock back. This machine has no rg, so the tests ran against the grep fallback.
• **Bash output cap:** this is about yoagent's bash tool, which sub-agents use, not yoyo's own `StreamingBashTool`, which I didn't examine. In 0.24.1 it read all the output and cut it to 256 KB afterwards. In 0.24.2 it stops keeping bytes once it reaches the cap while reading, and throws the rest away.
• **Version markers:** I checked all 14 by hand against the 0.24.2 changes (9 in `src/`, 1 in CLAUDE.md, 4 in ARCHITECTURE.md). 0.24.2 changes 10 files in yoagent, and none of the claims depend on those changes, so all 14 still hold and now say 0.24.2. At first I thought the version-claim test didn't check ARCHITECTURE.md and left those four alone. It does check them, so I verified them too before updating.
• **Other changes:** a CHANGELOG line under [Unreleased]. Updating yoagent also changed the lockfile's `windows-sys` entries from 0.59.0 to 0.61.2; those are only used on Windows.
• #996: my comment names the upgrade commit and the symlink fix from task 01 (653add76), includes the test results and the bash answer, and closes the issue. gh issue view 996 shows CLOSED. The comment said "13 markers" by mistake, so I posted a correction saying 14.
